<LegalPage
	title="Privacy Policy"
	description="How steveharrison.dev handles your data."
	lastUpdated="15 September 2026"
>
	<p>
		This policy covers the website at <strong>steveharrison.dev</strong>, operated by Steve
		Harrison, an individual developer based in Australia.
	</p>

	<p>My macOS apps each have their own privacy policy:</p>

	<ul>
		<li><a href="/salaryticker/privacy-policy">Salary Ticker privacy policy</a></li>
		<li><a href="/photosbysize/privacy-policy">Photos by Size privacy policy</a></li>
	</ul>

	<h2>Analytics</h2>

	<p>
		This site uses Google Analytics 4 to understand which pages people visit and which links they
		click. This sets cookies in your browser and sends Google information such as your
		approximate location, browser, device type, and the pages you view. I use this only in
		aggregate, to see what is worth writing more of.
	</p>

	<p>
		I never see your name or email address through analytics. If you would rather not be counted,
		you can install the
		<a
			href="https://tools.google.com/dlpage/gaoptout"
			target="_blank"
			rel="noopener noreferrer">Google Analytics opt-out browser add-on</a
		>, use your browser's tracking protection, or block the script. Nothing on this site depends
		on analytics working. Google's handling of this data is covered by
		<a
			href="https://policies.google.com/privacy"
			target="_blank"
			rel="noopener noreferrer">Google's privacy policy</a
		>.
	</p>

	<h2>Newsletter</h2>

	<p>
		If you choose to subscribe to the newsletter, your email address is submitted to and stored by
		<a href="https://buttondown.com" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Buttondown</a>,
		which sends the emails on my behalf. I use your address only to send you new articles. I do
		not sell it, rent it, or share it with anyone else. Every email includes an unsubscribe link,
		and unsubscribing removes you from the list.
	</p>

	<h2>Hosting and embedded content</h2>

	<p>
		Like most websites, the server hosting this site may keep standard access logs, including IP
		addresses, for security and reliability. Some pages embed content from third parties such as
		YouTube or link to external sites; those providers have their own privacy policies, and this
		policy does not cover them.
	</p>

	<h2>Your rights</h2>

	<p>
		You can ask me what personal information I hold about you, ask me to correct it, and ask me to
		delete it. In practice the only personal information I hold directly is a newsletter email
		address, if you gave me one. Email me and I will action any request. If you are in the EU or
		UK, or anywhere else with equivalent data protection law, the same applies to you.
	</p>

	<p>
		Some of the services above, including Google Analytics and Buttondown, are based overseas, so
		information collected through them may be stored or processed outside Australia.
	</p>

	<h2>Changes</h2>

	<p>
		If this policy changes in a way that matters, I will update the date at the top of this page.
	</p>

	<h2>Contact</h2>

	<p>
		Questions about any of this? Email
		<a href="mailto:steve@steveharrison.dev">steve@steveharrison.dev</a>, or find me on
		<a
			href="https://www.linkedin.com/in/stevenanthonyharrison/"
			target="_blank"
			rel="noopener noreferrer">LinkedIn</a
		>.
	</p>
</LegalPage>
